Stage-4 macros: a name defined twice in a block is an error; the replicated counts no longer spell like the tier estimates

The count of replicated T1 tiers was named RepTOneSame, the same name as the T1 estimate of the tier
called same, and silently overwrote it. Each stage-4 block now builds its macros in a table that
refuses a second definition (the counts are RepTOneReplicated, RepTThreeReplicated,
RepTFourReplicated), with a test; paper/generated regenerated.

